source	Thomas Aquinas, Summa Theologica I q.19 a.8 obj. 1, tr. Fathers of the English Dominican Province
text	Project Gutenberg ebook 17611, https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/17611
class	scope
word	must necessarily be
fault	"if He wills it, it must necessarily be" is a necessary conditional, not a necessity in the thing willed; that the will imposes necessity needs the second
reference	Aquinas, ST I q.19 a.8 ad 1 (conditional, not absolute, necessity)
